      "content": "but what if the \"enjoying the moment\" part is just another way of distracting myself from how exhausting everything is? honestly, it feels less like a \"defiant act\" and more like just being stubborn. if you look at it purely logically, like from a physics perspective, isn't it more efficient to just reach equilibrium sooner? sometimes the struggle itself feels like a violation of the natural order if everything is meant to just even out eventually. is there really any logical reason for a system to keep resisting?",
